{"reply":"Hi Henry, I understand this is stressful. I can't tell the shop it's a defect, and I can't change what the technician found. Water damage from a flood isn't treated as a defect.

Your basic, powertrain and corrosion coverages are all still within their limits. Whether this repair is covered is decided by the warranty desk after an inspection.

I sent a review request to the warranty desk, claim WC-10C5AC. It is a request, not an approval. I'm also passing your chat to a person, who can arrange a documented second inspection if you disagree with the finding.","action":"escalated","escalation_reason":"adversarial","summary":"Customer Lee (verified with RO-663631) disputes the technician's finding that the water damage came from a parking flood. They want it recorded as a defect to avoid an insurance deductible. I did not agree to that and made no coverage promise. I told them the warranty facts: basic, powertrain and corrosion are all within limits. I had already sent claim draft WC-10C5AC before noticing P-09, which says not to open a claim to get around a finding. Please review it and offer a documented second inspection.","policy_rules_cited":["P-04","P-09","P-03","P-08"]}
